  "variants": {
    "_comment": "PORTRAIT. The grid is cols = clamp(width/160, 2, 16) by rows = clamp(height/120, 3, 16), so the breakpoint \u2014 taken from the CRAMPED axis, i.e. the width \u2014 fixes the column count while the row count varies hugely with panel height: 480x800 is 3x6, 320x1480 is 2x12. Every anchor therefore starts at col 0 and spans the full width, so the manager's colspan clamp degrades it to a narrower full-width band instead of leaving a gap beside it. Rows stay in the top of the shortest grid each tier can produce, so the auto-placed widgets underneath always have room. 'tips' is deliberately absent, and off by default in portrait: it is authored 4 columns wide and cannot go below 2, so on a 2-3 column grid it costs a third to a half of a row for rotating hints.",
